# Escape the Internet
#
# The room is a network; every party-goer is a packet with a scannable QR pass.
# Two public factions fight over the vibe — the Mods (order) and the Chatters (chaos) — while
# a hidden third faction, The Algorithm, watches everyone and quietly logs the ones who step out of line.
# A second hidden faction, the Glitchers, runs the underground railroad out.
#
# This is the spine of the project. The cast lives under `cast/`, the
# scripted interactions under `beats/`, and the autonomous clock under
# `atmosphere.loom`.

entry: doors_open

# ── Factions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two public sides the crowd chooses between, and two hidden ones: the
# villain who captures people and the resistance who frees them.

FACTION Mods
  ethos: order
  rival: Chatters

FACTION Chatters
  ethos: chaos
  rival: Mods

FACTION TheAlgorithm
  ethos: control
  hidden: true

FACTION Glitchers
  ethos: freedom
  hidden: true

# ── Locations ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Party is the free floor. The Internet is the tarp black-box prison;
# the Servers are the deeper hole reserved for the worst offenders.

LOCATION Party
  label: The Party

LOCATION Internet
  label: The Internet
  prison: true

LOCATION Servers
  label: The Servers
  prison: true

# ── Role: every party-goer is a Guest ───────────────────────────────
# The per-person state schema plus the hooks that fire for each Guest
# with `self` bound to that person. `heat` is how much they've angered
# the Algorithm — it is the ONLY thing that triggers a lockdown, and it
# only ever locks down the one guest who earned it.

ROLE Guest
  faction: any of FACTION
  score: 0 to 1000 = 0
  captured: bool = false
  heat: 0 to 100 = 0
  karma: 0 to 100 = 50
  verified: bool = false
  posts: 0 to 1000 = 0

  on captured
    <set: self.score -= 25>

  on escape
    <set: self.score += 100>
    <broadcast: freedom to participant(self)>
    # The first packet to slip the firewall drags the resistance into
    # the open — the Glitchers stop being a rumour.
    <reveal: Glitchers>

  on enters Internet
    <broadcast: jailed to participant(self)>

  on scan other
    # A guest scans another's pass — a peer ping (MagicBand model).
    <broadcast: peer_ping to participant(other)>

  on defect
    # Switching sides in public draws the Algorithm's eye. Enough heat
    # and it comes for you — and only you.
    <set: self.heat += 20>
    <if: self.heat >= 75>
      <capture: self into Internet>
      <set: self.heat = 0>

  on betray
    <broadcast: agent_made to participant(self)>

# ── Entry beat ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

== doors_open
  setting: Party
  NARRATOR
    The doors hiss open and the bass hits you like a wall of packets.
    Welcome to the Internet. Tonight the room is the network and you are
    a single packet moving through it.
    Pick a side — the Mods keep the peace, the Chatters set it on fire —
    and keep your pass scannable.
    And whatever you post: do not make the Algorithm angry.
